[LEARNING PROJECT]

plank :- intrigrate btrfs snapshot to systemd-boot

it does few things like following:

- make bootloader entries for snapshot it found.
- delete loader entries that no longer point to actual snapshot or kernel.
- allow list and view each bootloader entries (made by plank).
- check for kernel mismatch (see docs/kernelmismatch.txt).
- list subvolumes for given btrfs filesystem with additional info.
- give tree view of btrfs filesystem subvolumes which make it easy to
  see that who is parent and child in tree.

it currectly in development phace and it include lots
of strange ways to do things.(as i am learning) and of course
bugs.

